| Leaving Cursor but keeping VS Code | GitHub Copilot or Claude Code | Both run as extensions, so there is no new editor to learn |
| Wanting the closest editor replacement | Windsurf (Devin Desktop) | A full editor with Tab completions and agents |
| Wanting a native, non-VS Code editor | Zed | Native app, bring your own keys, external agents |
| Handing off long tasks | Claude Code or Codex | Agent-first, terminal and cloud runs |
| On a tight budget | Antigravity, Copilot Free or Zed Personal | Free plans with real agent or completion access |
| Wanting open source | Kilo Code (MIT) or the Codex CLI (Apache-2.0) | Licenses stated in the GitHub repos |
| A JetBrains user | JetBrains Junie, Copilot or Claude Code | Each has a documented JetBrains path |
| Running a team with specs and reviews | Kiro | Specs, steering files and shared credit pools |
| In a region with regional pricing | Trae | Lite plan in 12 listed countries |

## Common mistakes

1. **Comparing sticker prices only.** Cursor Plus at $8 cannot use third-party models, Copilot's agent use draws down credits, and Kiro and Trae meter usage in credits or dollars. Read what the plan includes.
2. **Assuming "free" means unlimited.** Antigravity's free plan is a weekly baseline quota with no published numbers, and Windsurf's free agent quota is "light."
3. **Trusting a roundup that still lists Void.** Its README says it is deprecated. Check the repo before you build a workflow on any tool.
4. **Ignoring where code goes.** Free routes such as Kilo's Auto Free depend on which free models are available, and Cursor's November post shows why you should read incident notes. Check each vendor's data terms before using private code.
5. **Moving all your rules by hand.** Use a shared AGENTS.md or a sync skill instead of rewriting rules per tool.
6. **Switching everything at once.** Trial one real task per tool for a week before you move a team.

## Buying and setup checklist

- [ ] List the three tasks you do most in Cursor (for example, multi-file refactors, quick edits, code review).
- [ ] Pick one editor-based and one agent-based alternative from this list and run the same task in each.
- [ ] Confirm the plan you would actually buy, and what happens when its allowance runs out.
- [ ] Check whether the tool is available in your country (Trae and Kiro both note regional limits on some models or plans).
- [ ] Copy your Cursor rules into AGENTS.md so every tool can read them.
- [ ] Check the vendor's data and privacy terms before pointing a tool at private code.
- [ ] Re-check prices on the vendor page the day you buy. Several vendors here have changed plans this year.

## How we evaluated

We did not benchmark these tools. For each product, on November 27, 2026, we read the vendor's pricing page, its docs, and (where it exists) its GitHub repository through the public page, and we recorded plan names, prices, free-tier terms, limits and licenses as they appear. We checked star counts on the same day. We confirmed that every link, image, YouTube video and X post used here resolves, and we confirmed that the YouTube title and the tweet authors match what the article says. We did not install or run any of these tools, and we ran none of the catalog skills.

What this means for you: statements about pricing, plans and licenses are as reliable as the vendor pages on the day we read them, and statements about which tool is "best" are our judgment from those pages, not a measured result. Several pages contradicted themselves or left numbers out (Copilot's third-party agent access, Windsurf's Teams pricing, Antigravity's quotas, Junie's paid prices). Where that happened we said so in the section instead of choosing a side.

We dropped one product, Void, because its own README says it is deprecated and no longer accepting contributions. We kept Windsurf because it is still sold, under the Devin Desktop name.

## FAQ

### What is the best AI code editor like Cursor?

It depends on what you liked about Cursor. If you want an editor that feels similar, Windsurf (now Devin Desktop) is the closest match we found. If you want to stay in VS Code, GitHub Copilot and Claude Code both run as extensions. If you want a native editor, Zed. If you mostly want agents, Claude Code and Codex. This ranking is our judgment, not a benchmark result.

### What is Cursor AI?

Cursor describes itself as "your coding agent for building ambitious software." It is an AI-first code editor and agent, with Cloud Agents, Automations, Bugbot for code review and a code-hosting product called Origin. As of November 27, 2026 it is part of SpaceX, according to Cursor's own August 14 post.

### What are Cursor AI's main features?

From Cursor's own pages and docs: an Agent that edits across files, Cloud Agents and Automations, code review with Bugbot, MCP support, its own models (Grok 4.7, Grok 4.6, Grok 4.5 and Composer 2.5) and, since October, Computer Use for clicking and typing across desktop apps. Plan limits vary, and the Plus plan has no third-party models and no Cloud Agents.

### What is the most reliable AI code editor in 2026?

We cannot name one. We found no neutral reliability benchmark that covers these products, and vendor claims are not comparable. What we can say is which signals are checkable: a maintained product, a published pricing page, a stated license, and a clear ownership line. Every tool here met those tests except where noted, and Void failed the first one.

### Are there free alternatives to Cursor?

Yes. Google Antigravity has a free individual plan with a weekly baseline quota. GitHub Copilot Free gives 2,000 completions a month plus limited agent use. Windsurf's free plan has unlimited Tab and inline edits. Zed's Personal plan is free with your own keys or external agents. Kilo Code is free software with inference billed separately. Kiro gives 50 credits a month. Trae has a limited free plan. Codex is included on ChatGPT Free, subject to rollout. For limits in detail, see our [free coding agents guide](https://agentskills.codes/blog/best-free-ai-coding-agents-2026).

### What is the cheapest paid alternative?

On sticker price: Trae Lite at $8 (12 listed countries only), then GitHub Copilot Pro and Zed Pro at $10, then Windsurf, Kiro, Trae and Claude Code Pro at $20 (Claude Pro is $17 a month if billed annually). For comparison, Cursor Plus is $8 but runs only Cursor's own models. The cheapest plan is not always the cheapest way to finish a task, because included usage differs.

### Which Cursor alternatives are open source?

Kilo Code (MIT license on the GitHub repo) and the Codex CLI (Apache-2.0) are the clearest. Zed's pricing page describes the editor as open source, and its GitHub repo lists the license as "Other." Claude Code's GitHub repo lists no license, and Junie's repo says "All rights reserved." Void was open source but is deprecated.

### Is Void still maintained?

No. The README says "Void is now deprecated" and that it is no longer accepting contributions. The code remains online and had 28,699 GitHub stars on November 27, 2026, but we do not recommend building on it.

### Is Windsurf still called Windsurf?

Windsurf is now Devin Desktop, according to Devin's own post "Windsurf is now Devin Desktop," and the windsurf.com pricing page is titled "Devin Plans and Pricing." The Windsurf name is still widely used in search, so we use both.

### Do I have to leave VS Code to leave Cursor?

No. GitHub Copilot, Claude Code, Codex and Kilo Code all offer VS Code extensions or integrations, according to their docs and README files. Only Zed and Trae's IDE window are separate editors in this list (Trae's IDE window supports VS Code extensions), and Antigravity ships its own app.

### Which alternative is best for JetBrains users?

JetBrains Junie runs inside JetBrains IDEs and as a CLI. GitHub Copilot lists JetBrains IDEs as supported, and Claude Code's docs mention a JetBrains plugin. Kilo Code lists a JetBrains extension, and the Windsurf site says its JetBrains plugin remains available for download. Junie's paid prices were not available on the pages we could read.

### Can I reuse my Cursor rules in other tools?

Mostly. Copy the content into AGENTS.md, which the Codex README and several other tools read, or keep a CLAUDE.md for Claude Code. The catalog skills agent-conf-sync and agent-md-refactor in the block above help with the move, and our [rules-file guide](https://agentskills.codes/blog/agents-md-vs-claude-md-vs-skill-md-vs-cursor-rules) explains the formats.

### How often do these prices change?

Often. Cursor's plan structure has changed this year and now labels the old plans "legacy," and Windsurf has been renamed. Treat every number here as valid on November 27, 2026 and re-check the vendor page before buying.

